{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1386899-2e-harmony-questions","id":1386899,"title":"[2E] Harmony Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-08T21:15:11-07:00","id":1386899,"title":"[2E] Harmony Questions","content":"You were sure it will come, sooner or later... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have not clear image on one thing - and surely next will come with this.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Is Tribal Oath permanent Ban Condition on particular Uratha? </b>I ask as one PC in our game have lowered Harmony to Ban territory ( Harmony 4 ). His Tribal Oath would make great Ban Condition to him. However, I'm not sure if Tribal Oath, de facto, <i>already</i> the Ban of all Tribes characters - only it's not written for all of them on sheets. <b>Rephrasing the question then - Is Tribal Oath hard ( rules-wise ) Ban Condition on everyone - or just guidance for tribes characters?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-09-2020, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T10:19:53-07:00","id":1387008,"title":"","content":"It's not a Ban Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T22:41:27-07:00","id":1388234,"title":"","content":"So I <b><i>can</i></b> give players Ban based on the Tribal Oath - only by breaking then Tribal Oath, they get Breaking Point to Flesh <b>and</b> Ban repercussions. Cool! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T11:26:27-07:00","id":1394822,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">I searched the Core book for all &quot;breaking point towards X&quot; and found these, besides the list next to Harmony on page 104. Seems to me like you might be interrested in adding it to your very useful Hacks Hub. <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spirit</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">WtF 131</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nature</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">BEAST RIDE (WISDOM)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Should the animal be killed while she is riding, she is ejected back to her own body and treats it as a breaking point towards Spirit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">WtF 135</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Technology</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">IRON SLAVE (WISDOM)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Should the vehicle or machine be destroyed while the Uratha is riding it, she is ejected back into her own body and treats it as a breaking point towards Spirit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">WtF 141</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rite</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">SACRED HUNT (\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the Uratha bring down a spirit that is the prey of this rite, they may divide its remaining Essence amongst themselves as they see fit; this can be used to destroy a spirit by draining all its Essence and discorporating it, but doing so is usually a breaking point toward Spirit and is seen as disrespectful if done without good reason.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">WtF 144</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rite</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">TOTEMIC EMPOWERMENT</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Being empowered by the totem is a breaking point toward Spirit for an Uratha, and an Integrity breaking point for a human or Wolf-Blooded.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Flesh</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">WtF 108</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">SELF-CONTROL (\u2022\u2022) Prerequisites: Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: Your character can stave off her spirit nature. When compelled to shift in a stressful situation due to low Harmony (see p. 96), you may spend a point of Willpower to allow her to remain in her current form for the scene. Doing so is a breaking point toward Flesh.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">WtF 138</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Change</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">THE FATHER\u2019S FORM (PURITY)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Further, taking Gauru form and not engaging in combat goes against Father Wolf\u2019s ancient expectations; shifting to another form to end this Facet is a breaking point towards Flesh.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">WtF 165</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">FORCING DOORS</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To make things easier for the persuading character, he can apply Hard Leverage \u2014 a catch-all euphemism for threats, intimidation, drugging, blackmail, and other heavy-handed forms of coercion. If the persuader uses a form of Hard Leverage, it\u2019s a breaking point towards Flesh.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24678-yaydee","name":"YayDee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T00:37:50-07:00","id":1395030,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24678-yaydee\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24678\" data-vbnamecard=\"24678\">YayDee</a> - I love this compilation! I very much thank you for that! And it's just now added to Hubs by being in this topic - as rest of X Questions series. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}